    {
      "id": "ds9R9JH8WMqDottUex-HX",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 351,
      "y": 3406,
      "width": 957,
      "height": 350,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "an",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1146178455,
      "version": 544,
      "versionNonce": 456821591,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1787670018195,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "You can't \"monkey patch\" JavaScript. You can replace and add new APIs, but can't change\nthe language.\n\nJavaScript language ways of handling async\n    - events with callbacks. add a pointer to a function to run *later*\n    - Chris Quall - 'Promises' - \n\n\n\nconst data = await svc.getData();  // promises are \"thenables\" \n\nconsole.log(\"Here's the data\", data);\n\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "You can't \"monkey patch\" JavaScript. You can replace and add new APIs, but can't change\nthe language.\n\nJavaScript language ways of handling async\n    - events with callbacks. add a pointer to a function to run *later*\n    - Chris Quall - 'Promises' - \n\n\n\nconst data = await svc.getData();  // promises are \"thenables\" \n\nconsole.log(\"Here's the data\", data);\n\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "neXlIRi7rTJ9fxzLa3Yg8",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 341,
      "y": 3770,
      "width": 759,
      "height": 275,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "ao",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 327525657,
      "version": 478,
      "versionNonce": 1232658519,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1787670398378,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "- Another way to handle asynchronous stuff (other than promises)\nis using rxjs (reactive extensions for JavaScript)\n\n- reach for an observable (rxjs, effects in ngrx, etc.)\n    - when you need a promise that keeps on giving.\n    - when a bunch of \"thens\" chained together would be misery.\n    - when the data from the venue outside your app returns data that\n      is vastly different from the needs of your app.\n\n\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "- Another way to handle asynchronous stuff (other than promises)\nis using rxjs (reactive extensions for JavaScript)\n\n- reach for an observable (rxjs, effects in ngrx, etc.)\n    - when you need a promise that keeps on giving.\n    - when a bunch of \"thens\" chained together would be misery.\n    - when the data from the venue outside your app returns data that\n      is vastly different from the needs of your app.\n\n\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
